The QA-layer audit reports 7 SILENT_NON_FIRING and 1 REAL_BUG in
adversarial_verify.py itself, regenerated cleanly yesterday evening, and the
conductor has been emitting AUDIT_FINDING_UNTRIAGED for them with one now open
seven days. The audit found them; nobody has acted.

The sharpest is _is_deterministic_verifier handing an artifact that declares
live_llm_inference_with_metamorphic_replay at duration_s 0.080581 the
0.0001-second deterministic floor, with no duration flag. An artifact claiming
live LLM inference in eighty milliseconds passes the gate built after exp1851
fabricated TPR 1.0 in 3.4 seconds. The other six each name a concrete corpus
input the same way.

Written separately from the report because of what it means in aggregate: three
independent findings of this one bug class landed today -- the ARC floor check
scoping on arc inside research, the FAIL message using one path's token for
both, and these seven. The class is common here and is not being triaged as it
arrives.

Not actioned. Widening adversarial_verify changes what the entire corpus is
judged against, a wrong widening quarantines honest work and a timid one leaves
the hole, and the audit deliberately never edits. Sequencing is the operator's.
The entry adds no information the report lacks; it records that the findings are
open, aging, and share a class with two discoveries made independently today.

